{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_28_1109794141#0_2372669788","relevance":0,"reason":"The passage states the opposite of the information need: free or discounted items can increase perceived value and generosity, and it is about birthday freebies rather than why free things are perceived as less valuable.","learned":"Queries around 'when something is free' and 'perceived value' can retrieve marketing freebies that argue free increases value, not decreases it."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"people value what they pay for\" free)","reason":"This common phrase is likely to retrieve direct explanations that paying creates commitment/value while free offerings are undervalued."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"people value what they pay for\" free)"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_52_637187850#17_1217773000","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q3877","rank":1,"snippet":"and iterate once you’re live About the author Topics: Join 446,005 entrepreneurs who already have a head start. Email address Start your 14-day <cover>free trial today! \" , \"segment\": \"The problem si this - we're going to be marketing an e-course on mindfulness and brain training. It's 12 weeks, includes over 50 audios, several dozen videos, 100 pages of text, and offers infographics and other extras as well. The conventional wisdom is that this kind of course would go for 150 or $200. The problem is, that would limit it to a relatively small market of mental health professionals and possibly teachers who use mindfulness in education. We think there's a much bigger market (the 40-50% of college students who are struggling with anxiety and depression, for example) that just is not going to spend over $100 for a course. We're inclined toward something like $50-60 but we also keep hearing the conventional observation that \\\"people value what they pay for.\\\" </cover>So, any insights would be most welcome. Thanks!! see more − + LIVIN' LIFE ® donsalmon • 3 years ago We would say put yourself your target markets shoes. "}}
